Option B: conflictReworkScan.js exports `sliceCap(rule, limit, fallthroughReserve)`. This keeps githubSource slimmer and is more testable. The PR description says the budget module is "shared by smAgent.js and githubSource.js". Adding the slice-cap choice there fits: it's the conflict-rework-aware cap.

I'll go with Option B: add to conflictReworkScan.js:

```js
// gh-1027 (CRAP refactor): the per-rule candidate-slice cap, extracted
// from queryPrs so its complexity doesn't compound the query function.
// conflict_rework widens to the shared over-scan budget; every other rule
// keeps the gh-922 fallthrough reserve.
function sliceCap(rule, limit, fallthroughReserve) {
   if (rule && rule.localAction === 'conflict_rework') {
       return scanLimit(limit);
   }
   return (typeof limit === 'number' ? limit : 0) + fallthroughReserve;
}
```

Careful about the non-conflict path: original was `limit + TRIGGER_FALLTHROUGH_RESERVE`. limit could be non-number? queryPrs callers pass a number limit. Keep same semantics: `limit + fallthroughReserve`.

